+### M1 private fixed-sequence diagnostic provider and receipt
+
+`OPENWEPP_COLD_M1_FIXED_SEQUENCE_PROVIDER_V1` is the sole private prescribed
+provider for the two M1 cycles.  It is neither the climate-derived
+`SC-SNOWFREEFORCING-001` provider nor a meteorological model, and changes no
+physical scalar, solar/radiation, GSI, or warm start.  The payload is canonical
+ASCII JSON: UTF-8 ASCII subset only; recursively lexicographic keys; no
+whitespace except one final LF; slash is unescaped; quote is `\"`, backslash
+is `\\`, and every U+0000..U+001F control is lowercase `\u00xx`; all other
+escape spellings and non-ASCII code points reject. Duplicate/unknown keys reject.
+JSON Pointer uses RFC 6901 `~0`/`~1` decoding and selects exactly one value.
+Integers are canonical base-10 without sign/leading zero; all emitted floats
+are exactly 16 lowercase hexadecimal IEEE-754 binary64 bits.  Source file
+hashes retain lexical provenance, so no source decimal-token grammar is reused.
+
+The closed top-level schema is `schema_version:u32=1`, `provider_id:String`,
+`calendar:CalendarV1`, `cycle:CycleV1`,
+`sources:[SourceV1]`, `implementation:ImplementationV1`, and
+`forcing_projection:ProjectionV1`.  `CalendarV1` has exactly
+`system:"proleptic_gregorian"`, `fixed_utc_offset_seconds:0`,
+`day_seconds:86400`, `daylight_saving:false`, `leap_seconds:false`,
+`origin:"2000-06-20T00:00:00+00:00"`, `tick_unit:"integer_nanoseconds"`, and
+`day_mapping:[DayV1;3]`, where each `DayV1` has exactly `day_ordinal:u32` and
+`civil_date:String`: `{0,"2000-06-20"}`, `{1,"2000-06-21"}`, and
+`{2,"2000-06-22"}`. `cycle_clock_resets:true` is an exact `CalendarV1` member.
+Each `CycleV1` has exactly `ordinal:u32`, `id:String`, and
+`initial_phase_records:[InitialPhaseV1]`; `InitialPhaseV1` has exactly
+`occupancy_id:String`, `mass_kg_m2_tile_ground:binary64_bits`, and
+`enthalpy_j_m2_tile_ground:binary64_bits`. The ordered cycles are ordinal zero
+`original_liquid_cold_thaw_refreeze_warm`, then ordinal one
+`distinct_phase_inventory_shifted_cycle`. Ordinal, id, initial phases, and the real independent
+seven-owner beginning set must agree before construction; that owner set remains
+the non-circular coupled-time `begin_owner_set` input.
+
+Each `SourceV1` has exactly `name`, `repository_relative_path`, and lowercase
+`sha256`; the array begins with these two mandatory entries, in this order:
+original input
+`docs/work-packages/20260920-cold-canopy-m1-001/artifacts/original-input-reference.json`
+`4b324b0a9c136f2203e8073ca260db5be9e7dd07722a37aec60f2cd528be2d54`; then
+continuous fixture
+`docs/work-packages/20260920-cold-canopy-m1-001/artifacts/continuous-fixtures-draft01.json`
+`8cf391055e107ca854f72fb1f70a0e78298575ad0d2ede6fa6c9c760c18191e1`.
+Additional entries are admitted only for retained source-extraction adapters
+and their dependency manifests. Hashes are checked before parsing.
+`ImplementationV1` has exactly
+`provider_version`, `repository_relative_path`, and lowercase `sha256` for the
+selected expansion source; an unbound provider label rejects.
+
+`ProjectionV1` has exactly `projection_id:"OPENWEPP_COLD_M1_PIECEWISE_CONSTANT_V1"`, `support_unit:"s"`,
+`support_seconds:60`, `cycle_id`, `segments`, `records`, and `source_joins`.
+Each segment has exactly `ordinal`, `start_ns`, `end_ns`, and `overrides`; its
+`overrides` has exactly `air_temperature_k`, `air_specific_humidity_kg_kg`,
+`atmospheric_downward_longwave_w_m2`, `top_liquid_rate_kg_m2_tile_s`, and
+`top_liquid_temperature_k`, each binary64 bits.  Each record repeats that closed
+shape and has exactly `ordinal`, `start_ns`, `end_ns`, and `overrides`.
+The provider id is exactly `OPENWEPP_COLD_M1_FIXED_SEQUENCE_PROVIDER_V1`.
+Segments are contiguous, variable-duration half-open source ranges whose
+durations are divisible by 60 seconds; records are their contiguous fixed
+60-second expansion in source order. The first cycle preserves `[0,60)` then
+`[60,86400)`, and each cycle covers exactly `[0,259200000000000)` ns with
+records `0..4319`. Parent `n` is `u32` in `0..143`, selects exactly records
+`30n..30n+29`, and has support `[1800n,1800(n+1))` seconds; all tick strings
+are checked unsigned canonical decimal `u128` ns from the calendar origin and
+all full schedule breakpoints remain sealed.
+
+`source_joins` has exactly seven entries in this order: `current_gsi`,
+`exposure`, `destination`, `co2_pa`, `reference_height_m`, `topology`, and
+`controller_policy`. Each `SourceJoinV1` has exactly `field`, `source_path`,
+`source_sha256`, `locator_kind`, `locator`, `value_kind`, `value`, and
+`support_receipt_sha256`.
+`locator_kind` is `json_pointer` or `source_extraction_adapter`; `value_kind` is exactly
+`binary64_bits`, `utf8`, or `canonical_json_sha256`. A `json_pointer` locator
+is the RFC 6901 pointer above. A `source_extraction_adapter` locator is an
+`AdapterV1` object with exactly `adapter_path`, `adapter_sha256`,
+`dependency_manifest_path`, `dependency_manifest_sha256`,
+`constructor_accessor`, `output_canonical_json_sha256`, and `output_pointer`.
+It invokes only the named retained constructor/accessor, verifies every source
+in its dependency manifest, hashes the complete frozen constructor-output JSON,
+then applies `output_pointer`; regex/source-text evaluation or a new physical
+scalar rejects. The extracted value is then encoded exactly by `value_kind`:
+scalar bits, UTF-8 bytes, or canonical JSON bytes followed by SHA-256. Scalars (GSI, CO2, reference height) use binary64
+bits; destination uses UTF-8; exposure, topology, and controller use the SHA-256
+of their canonical structured value. A cardinality/order/kind/locator/path/hash/
+value/support-receipt mismatch rejects before receipt minting. For `current_gsi`,
+`support_receipt_sha256` is mandatory and the referenced receipt must bind the
+same run, cycle, `[start_ns,end_ns)`, and scalar bits; the receiver consumes it
+at `advance_m1_caller_support`, never the provisional zero placeholder. The
+retained endpoint fixture's scalar `1.0` and reference height `24` do not prove
+correspondence to the frozen M1 cycle and do not replace frozen original solver
+forcing. Original CO2 `42` and reference height `24` remain their own joins.
+
+Raw SHA-256 authenticates source content only. `payload_content_sha256` is the
+raw SHA-256 of the full canonical payload bytes (the payload has no run field).
+`run_identity` is derived with
+private domain `openwepp-m1-fixed-sequence-run-v1`, in this ordered frame:
+`schema_version:u32`, `provider_id:utf8`, `calendar:canonical_json`,
+`original_source_sha256:raw32`, `continuous_source_sha256:raw32`,
+`implementation_version:utf8`, `implementation_path:utf8`, and
+`implementation_sha256:raw32`, and `payload_content_sha256:raw32`.
+`calendar_receipt` uses private domain
+`openwepp-m1-fixed-sequence-calendar-provider-v1` and ordered fields
+`run_identity:raw32`, `cycle_ordinal:u32`, `cycle_id:utf8`, and
+`initial_phase_records:canonical_json`. `forcing_receipt` uses private domain
+`openwepp-m1-fixed-sequence-parent-forcing-v1` and ordered fields
+`calendar_receipt:raw32`, `full_projection_content_sha256:raw32`,
+`parent_ordinal:u32`, `support_start_ns:u128`,
+`support_end_ns:u128`, `record_count:u32`, and `ordered_records:canonical_json`.
+All three use `OPENWEPP_CANONICAL_FRAMED_SHA256_V1`; they are provider-owned
+domains, neither new nor repurposed coupled-time tags. The two latter raw32
+values feed existing coupled-time receipt fields.
+Admission rejects any mutation, omission, reorder, unknown/duplicate/noncanonical
+field, wrong source join, or projection mismatch as `VEG-E-144`, with no owner
+mutation. `OBL-VEGETATION-C-008` adds canonical-payload known-answer; every
+source/path/pointer/kind/value, calendar/run/cycle/phase, segment/record,
+breakpoint/support, implementation, and scalar-equality mutation; and requires
+no staged owner or parent publication on each rejection. A private receipt does
+not admit a parent; authentic unchanged snow remains the seventh owner.
+
